# This file is the machine readable definition of what counts as user material, which is why it is
# commented at length: getting it wrong is the one mistake in this project that cannot be undone
# by editing a file afterwards. The repository is public.
#
# Since D20 nothing specific to a user or an engagement lives in this folder at all: the
# configuration, the scenarios, the data and every run's output sit in the workspace next to it,
# ../clockwork-workspace, which Clockwork finds and creates by itself. The rules below are guards,
# in case any of it is ever recreated here by mistake.
#
# All project level rules are ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored pattern such
# as `blueprints/` matches at any depth and would also swallow `selftest/blueprints/`, which must
# be kept. And the `/*` form is required for a `!` exception to work at all, because git does not
# descend into an excluded directory. Verify with `git check-ignore`, never by reading.
/legacy-data-extract/
/legacy-exports/
/exports/
/blueprints/*
/data/*
/templates/

# A workspace created or copied inside the application folder by mistake.
/clockwork-workspace/
/workspace/

# Secrets and session material.
#
# The captured session (npm run auth, SESSION=saved only) is cookies belonging to a signed in user:
# exactly as sensitive as the password. The pattern is deliberately unanchored so it catches the
# file wherever anyone puts it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
storageState*.json
/.auth/
/auth/

# Runtime artifacts. Traces and HAR files can contain session tokens, and the conversion report
# quotes the source export verbatim. Real runs write all of these into the workspace; the rules
# stay as guards.
*.har
*.trace
trace.zip
/reports/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/videos/
/screenshots/

# The self test's own output: synthetic, regenerated by every run, never client material.
/selftest/.output/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright leftovers not already covered above.
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# Editor and operating system droppings.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Legacy, drafts and generated files set aside before publication. Never versioned.
/trash/
